```astro
---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Building Reliable Infrastructure with DevOps | Feranmi Dada"
	description="Practical lessons on building reliable infrastructure, automation and continuous delivery."
>
	<main class="article">
		<header class="article-header">
			<p class="eyebrow">DEVOPS</p>

			<h1>Building Reliable Infrastructure with DevOps</h1>

			<p class="subtitle">
				How automation, observability and continuous delivery help teams
				build systems that are easier to operate and improve.
			</p>

			<p class="date">September 2026 · Feranmi Dada</p>
		</header>

		<article class="content">
			<h2>Why reliability matters</h2>

			<p>
				Modern applications depend on infrastructure that needs to remain
				available, observable and maintainable. DevOps brings development
				and operations practices together to make software delivery more
				reliable and repeatable.
			</p>

			<h2>Automation changes the workflow</h2>

			<p>
				Manual infrastructure changes can introduce inconsistency and make
				troubleshooting difficult. Infrastructure as Code, CI/CD pipelines
				and containerization allow teams to standardize how applications
				and infrastructure are built and deployed.
			</p>

			<h2>Observability is part of reliability</h2>

			<p>
				Deploying an application is only one part of the job. Teams also
				need visibility into system health. Metrics, logs and alerts help
				engineers identify problems and respond before they become larger
				incidents.
			</p>

			<h2>Continuous improvement</h2>

			<p>
				DevOps is not simply about using a collection of tools. The larger
				goal is to create a reliable delivery process where teams can
				measure results, learn from incidents and continuously improve
				their systems.
			</p>

			<div class="back">
				<a href="/blog">← Back to Blog</a>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
